[3A. Setter / Transition Evidence]: The `date_time` objects being compared are created by parsing a TOML string. The fuzz target constructs this string by conditionally appending hardcoded key-value pairs. The relevant lines are:
```cpp
if (fdp.ConsumeBool()) {
  toml_string += "\nldt1 = 1979-05-27T07:32:00\n";
}
if (fdp.ConsumeBool()) {
  toml_string += "\nodt1 = 1979-05-27T07:32:00-07:00\n";
}
```
Both of these hardcoded strings specify the exact same time: `07:32:00`. The fuzzer can decide whether to include one, both, or neither, but it cannot change the time values themselves. Consequently, any two `date_time` objects parsed from this input will have identical `time` members.
